{
  "version": 4,
  "notes": [
    "Each segment is removed from everything the PARENT model sees (system prompt sections, <rules>, tool declarations, tool results, injected wakes) by harness/ablation-ext.ts. Texts must match the extension source exactly; e2e/ablation-harness.test.ts fails on drift, and the runner marks an episode 'vacuous' when a requested segment never matched.",
    "A text/regex segment without text or pattern is the span marked <!--seg:id-->…<!--/seg--> in extension/prompts/ (see extension/prompts/INDEX.md); only segments that are not a prompt span (structural XML) keep a pattern here.",
    "Guidelines bullets and tool promptGuidelines overlap on purpose. They stay separate segments so the eval can tell which copy (if either) is load-bearing.",
    "scope=child / ablatable=false: text that only child sessions see. By design, children load no extensions, so no hook of the ablation harness runs there. The self-test still guards these texts against drift (checked in child calls), but the runner never schedules them as variants and the report lists them as 'not ablatable'.",
    "affects: scenarios where removing the segment is expected to matter. The runner tests only these pairs unless --pairs all. The control segment runs everywhere and must never come out load-bearing.",
    "kind=text: remove exact text (a bullet left empty is dropped). kind=regex: remove every match. kind=hook: mechanism disabled by the harness. kind=config: mechanism disabled via $PI_FAMULUS_HOME/config.json."
  ],
